= The 60-Second Self-Test

Cover the answers, say each one aloud, then check. If any answer takes longer than ten seconds, revisit that section.

- *The five Panchsheel principles?* → Sovereignty respect, non-aggression, non-interference, equality-mutual benefit, peaceful co-existence (1954, with China).
- *Name NAM's founding five and first summit.* → Nehru, Nasser, Tito, Sukarno, Nkrumah — Belgrade 1961.
- *The two fronts of the 1962 war?* → Aksai Chin (Ladakh) and the McMahon Line (NEFA); China attacked 20 Oct 1962; Menon resigned.
- *1965's chain in one breath?* → Kutch skirmishes → Operation Gibraltar → September war → Tashkent (10 Jan 1966) → Shastri dies.
- *Why did 80 lakh refugees matter in 1971?* → Searchlight's crackdown sent them to India — the emergency that forced Delhi's hand.
- *The Indo-Soviet Treaty: when and why?* → August 1971, BEFORE the war — 20 years; it deterred US-China intervention.
- *What happened on 16 December 1971 and in July 1972?* → Dhaka falls (Bangladesh born); Shimla Agreement renames the ceasefire line the Line of Control.
- *Pokhran-I: date, codename, official phrase?* → 18 May 1974; Smiling Buddha; "peaceful nuclear explosion".

